course: dictionary
lesson: 2987
title: Dug: the past of dig
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dig is an action word, and dug is its past form. Today we dig; yesterday we dug. Only dug is the past form, so never write digged. Scientists also use dug after have or has: «Long before scientists understood any of this, a girl called Mary Anning ... dug out the first complete ichthyosaur at about 12.»
explain: Dug has three main meanings. First, it means made a hole in the ground with a spade, hands or paws. Second, it means searched for and found something, as in «I dug out my old toys.» Third, it means pushed something into something, as in «the cat dug its claws in.»
explain: Check the sentence to find the meaning. If the story is about soil, holes or treasure, dug probably means made a hole or searched. If the story is about claws or nails, dug probably means pushed in. Your meaning should always make sense when you read the whole sentence.
fact: Dig, digs, digging and dug all belong to the same word.
fact: «Dug» is the past form of dig, so it tells you the digging happened before now.
fact: Phrases with dug: dug up, dug out, dug a hole and dug in.
fact: «Six feet under» means dead and buried, because graves were dug about six feet deep.
fact: Safety: do not dig near cables, pipes or deep in sand, because sand holes on beaches can collapse.
exercise: Yesterday the gardeners ___ holes to plant the seeds. | digging | *dug | dig | digs
exercise: Find the past form of dig in this sentence: «A canal is a waterway dug by people.» | digging | *dug | dig | digs
exercise: «The cat dug its claws in.» What does dug in mean here? | It washed its claws clean | It searched and found its claws | It made a hole in the ground | *It pushed its claws into something
test: Which sentence is correct? | The pirates digs for treasure yesterday | The pirates dig for treasure yesterday | *The pirates dug for treasure | The pirates digged for treasure
test: What does dug up mean? | Climbed up high | Washed clean | *Found by digging it out of the ground | Filled with water
exam: Why should you not dig near cables or pipes? | Because worms live there | *Because you could hit them and cause harm | Because the soil is too hard to move | Because it is always too wet
